[b]Single player only. Build 42.[/b]
Requires [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3803984183]Project A-Life[/url].

Fix or set your Project A-Life reputation from one small window. Made for the NPC who steps into your shot at a zombie: undo the kill and the grudges that came with it, nudge your score, forgive whole factions, or set what any one NPC thinks of you.

[h2]How to use[/h2]
[list]
[*]Click the small Rep: (your level) button below the clock in the top right. Drag it anywhere, or right-click it to hide it.
[*]Or right-click the world and choose Reputation editor. With the button hidden, the same menu has Show reputation button.
[*]The game pauses while the window is open and goes back to its old speed when you close it.
[*]Adjust by -100, -25, -5, +5, +25 or +100, or use Set level to jump to any of A-Life's eleven levels.
[*]Recent kills lists your last six NPC kills, each with Undo. Undo takes back the score loss, the faction turning hostile, the grudges and the pending revenge. Reputation earned since is kept.
[*]Factions shows each faction's attitude toward you, with Forgive and Make hostile, plus Forgive everyone.
[*]The People tab lists everyone with an opinion of you, from Hates you to Would stand by you. Pick someone to adjust it, set it to any label, make them forget you, calm them down or make them hostile.
[*]Join my crew makes anyone on the People tab one of your A-Life companions, no conversation needed. A-Life's limit of five still applies; Leave my crew lets them go.
[*]The Crew tab sets each companion's nine A-Life skills and their strength and accuracy (0 to 10, or Max everything), and changes their loadout: give any item in the game, hand them a weapon to hold with ammo, dress them, or take things back.
[*]Right-click an NPC and choose Edit relationship to jump straight to them.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Written against Project A-Life 1.5.2. Needs Build 42.21 or later.
[*]Works in existing saves. Kills are recorded from when you enable it; fix older ones with Adjust, Set level and Forgive.
[*]Single player only.
[/list]

[h2]Known issues[/h2]
[list]
[*]An NPC already fighting you that second keeps at it until A-Life's short combat memory (about 10 seconds) runs out.
[*]A revenge contract already sworn is called off on A-Life's next tick, but only for factions that aren't hostile to you by default.
[*]Set level doesn't count toward A-Life's highest-level-reached icons.
[*]Join my crew only reaches people near enough to be loaded in the world, and gear can only change while they're nearby.
[*]Of A-Life's nine companion skills, only first aid changes what they do; the others show on the Companions sheet. Strength and accuracy are what change how they fight.
[*]An NPC's opinion you set drifts back toward their usual feeling a few points a day, as all A-Life opinions do.
[/list]

Source and bug reports: [url=https://github.com/maxcwolf/pz-mods/tree/main/alife-rep-editor]GitHub[/url]
